course: dictionary
lesson: 15396
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can tell which meaning the writer means by reading the words around it. The word spirits is a good example: it can mean ghosts, moods, or liquids.
explain: «The old castle was haunted by spirits that drifted through the halls at midnight.» The clues are haunted and midnight, so spirits means ghosts. Now read «The team was in high spirits after winning the match.» The clue is winning, so spirits means mood here.
explain: Always check: does your meaning fit the sentence? If a word has a meaning you do not expect, try the other meanings one by one. The one that makes sense is the right one.
explain: Some spirits are not for children. Strong alcohol is called spirits, and white spirit is a poisonous cleaning liquid that burns easily. If you see this word on a label or a warning, ask an adult straight away.
fact: Spirits is the plural of spirit, so it can mean more than one spirit or ghost.
fact: «Her spirits lifted when she heard the good news.» Here spirits means mood or feelings.
fact: In high spirits means happy and full of energy; in low spirits means sad.
fact: Strong alcoholic drinks such as whisky, vodka and gin are called spirits. They are for adults only, never for children.
fact: White spirit and methylated spirits are poisonous cleaning liquids that burn easily, so keep well away from them.
exercise: «The old house was haunted by spirits who floated through the halls.» What does spirits mean here? | Cleaning liquids | *Ghosts | Team mates | Strong drinks
exercise: «Mia was in low spirits after she lost her game.» What does spirits mean here? | Liquids for cleaning | Courage | *Mood or feelings | Ghosts
exercise: «Keep away from white spirit, because it is poisonous.» What kind of liquid is white spirit? | A sweet fizzy drink | A kind of soap for bath time | A cold drink for summer | *A poisonous cleaning liquid
test: «The team showed great spirit and never gave up.» What does spirit mean here? | *Courage and energy | Strong alcohol | Ghosts | A kind of soap
test: «Dad said the bottles of spirits in the cupboard are for adults only.» Why are they for adults only? | They are ghost stories | *They are strong alcoholic drinks, not for children | They are cleaning liquids | Spirits are only for picnics
exam: «Grandma said, "A cheerful song will lift your spirits."» What does lift your spirits mean? | To make you tired and cross | *To make you feel happier | To make you cleaner | To make you float like a ghost
